0 Finish Test Row - one real brick per real LDConfig finish
0 Name: finishes.ldr
0 Author: spex project (hand-authored placement data; not sourced from an official ldraw.org models/ release)
0 // M56's acceptance criterion in one file: nine real LDraw colour codes,
0 // chosen so that every finish keyword the official LDConfig.ldr actually
0 // uses appears exactly once, plus the two modifiers that are not finishes
0 // at all (ALPHA and LUMINANCE).
0 //
0 //   4   Red                    solid, opaque       the baseline brick
0 //   47  Trans_Clear            solid, ALPHA 128    transmission + ior
0 //   383 Chrome_Silver          CHROME              needs the environment
0 //   80  Metallic_Silver        METAL
0 //   142 Pearl_Light_Gold       PEARLESCENT         iridescence, NOT metal
0 //   256 Rubber_Black           RUBBER              nearly fully diffuse
0 //   132 Speckle_Black_Silver   MATERIAL SPECKLE    particle params carried
0 //   117 Glitter_Trans_Clear    MATERIAL GLITTER    glitter AND transparent
0 //   21  Glow_In_Dark_Opaque    LUMINANCE 15        emission
0 //
0 // MATTE_METALLIC is in LDraw's grammar but no colour in the current
0 // official file uses it, so it cannot appear here. See Finish's doc comment
0 // in crates/spex-ldraw/src/colors.rs.
0 //
0 // Two courses tall (2x24 LDU) so each finish has a lit top, a lit side and
0 // a shaded side to be judged by; 40 LDU apart so a 20 LDU brick has a real
0 // gap either side. LDraw is Y-down, so the upper course is at y = -24.
0 BFC CERTIFY CCW
1 4 -160 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3005.dat
1 4 -160 -24 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3005.dat
